# Working with dude

[`dude`](https://github.com/cubocicloide/dude) is the project CLI — a single
entry point for all development tasks. Run `dude help` for a live overview, and
`dude help <command>` (or `dude help <group> <sub>`) for a command's flags.

---

## Installation

`dude` is published on the public npm registry. What you install
globally is the tiny **launcher** (`@cubocicloide/dude-launcher`); it then runs
each project's *pinned* CLI + stack automatically — no manual version switching.

```bash
# 1. Install the launcher globally (the only global install).
npm install -g @cubocicloide/dude-launcher
```

Then, inside this project, provision the pinned toolchain (the launcher would
also do this on the first `dude` command, but doing it explicitly is clearer):

```bash
pnpm install      # installs the pinned @cubocicloide/dude CLI + stack
dude version      # verify the resolved CLI + stack versions
```


---

## Getting started

### First run

```bash
# Build images and start all services — required the very first time
dude up
```
{{#if withPostgres}}

`dude up` applies pending Alembic migrations automatically on every start, so
the schema is always current — but a fresh database has no data. Run
`dude reset` once after this first `dude up` to drop the database, re-apply
migrations, and seed demo users (see [Database](#database-migrations) below).
{{/if}}

From the second run onward:

```bash
dude up
```

Also re-run `dude up --build` whenever you change a `Dockerfile` or
`pyproject.toml`.

### Services

Once the stack is up, open these URLs:

| Service | URL | Notes |
|---------|-----|-------|
| **Frontend** | http://localhost:5173 | React + Vite — HMR active |
| **API** | http://localhost:8000 | FastAPI |
| **API reference** | http://localhost:8000/api/docs | Interactive reference (Scalar) |
| **OpenAPI schema** | http://localhost:8000/api/openapi.json | Raw schema (JSON) |
| **Health** | http://localhost:8000/api/health | JSON health check |
{{#if withCelery}}| **Flower** | http://localhost:5555 | Celery task monitor |
{{/if}}

### Hot reload

- **Frontend** — Vite HMR is active. Edit any file under `frontend/src/` and
  the browser updates instantly without a full page reload.
- **Backend** — Uvicorn runs with `--reload`. Edit any Python file under
  `backend/app/` and the API restarts automatically within ~1 second.

