## Database (migrations)

Schema changes are managed with Alembic. These commands run inside the backend
container.

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `dude reset` | Drop the database, re-apply all migrations, and seed demo data |
| `dude db makemigration --message "<text>"` | Autogenerate a new migration from model changes |
| `dude db migrate` | Apply all pending migrations (default target: `head`) |
| `dude db migrate --revision <rev>` | Migrate up to a specific revision |
| `dude db rollback` | Downgrade by one revision |
| `dude db rollback --revision <rev>` | Downgrade to a specific revision |

`dude reset` is the fastest way to get a clean database with demo data — use
it after the first `dude up`, or any time your local data gets into a bad
state. `dude up` alone only ever applies migrations; it never seeds data or
touches an existing database.

**Workflow** — after changing a SQLAlchemy model:

```bash
dude db makemigration --message "add users table"
dude db migrate
git add backend/app/migrations/
```
{{/if}}

