## Getting help

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `dude info` | Print environment diagnostics (OS, Node/pnpm/Docker, dude + stack versions) |
| `dude report` | File a bug report about dude itself (the CLI or a stack), with `dude info` attached |

Hit a bug in `dude` or in this stack, rather than in your own application code?
`dude report` attaches your `dude info` diagnostics automatically and either
files the issue via `gh` or opens a pre-filled browser form — no manual
copy-pasting.

